    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft, See Invisibility",
    "tactics": "Shade Walkers are assassins. They use Planar Step to close distance, strike from darkness, and retreat before retaliation. A Cooperative Shade Walker follows target priority without complaint. An Indifferent one picks whoever is standing in the most shadow.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Shadow Strike [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 8 + Melee Combat 4), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 9 damage (5 + 4 Str) + 3 Negative damage (Ignore DR)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 9 damage, DR halved (round up) + 3 Negative damage; target is Disoriented until start of their next turn.</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 3:</strong> 9 damage, DR halved (round up) + 3 Negative damage; target Disoriented and loses the Hidden condition if they had it.</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Shadow Meld: In dim light or darkness, the Shade Walker has Fortune on Stealth. ### Attacks against it add 1 to both dice. Planar Step (1/short rest): As a [Move] action, the Shade Walker steps briefly into the Shadow Plane and re-emerges up to 30 feet away in any dim or dark location it can see. This movement does not provoke opportunity ### Attacks. Sunlight Sensitivity: In bright light, the Shade Walker adds 1 to both attack dice.</p>",
